                "ogg",
                "pcm",
                "adpcm",
                "alac",
                "aiff",
                "caf"
              ]
            }
          },
          "note": "Bevy's optional features for games and animation, behind the cargo feature bevy: only the plugin build gets them. shader_format_glsl and shader_format_wesl are gone in 0.20. custom_cursor is on for 0.20: bevy_feathers turns on bevy_window's half through bevy_picking, and hanabi's x11 brings bevy_winit, which fails to compile without its half. bevy_audio plays to the device, not into raea's mixer, so the engine leaves its AudioPlugin out (a TypeScript App can open it: plugins [\"bevy_audio\"]); symphonia's vorbis/ogg/alac/aiff join raea-media's decoders (raea's audio path) by feature unification. Left off: dlss (NVIDIA), hotpatching and dynamic_linking (dev builds), trace_* (profiling builds), webgl2/webgpu/web (wasm), x11/wayland/winit (raea draws headless), glam_assert (glam features broke 0.20 once), and the pbr_*_textures (transmission, multi_layer_material, anisotropy, specular, clustered_decals, light): each adds texture and sampler bindings to StandardMaterial, and on Metal, where bindless is off, its opaque pipeline then needs 24 samplers against the limit of 16, so the layout is invalid and the 3D pass draws nothing (10-24, P26 build/physics blank); turn them on only on a device with bindless. vox leaves its pbr_transmission_textures off for the same reason"
        },
